# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The image CMD is a boot wrapper that starts the vulnerable daemon(s) and then
# execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the service is ALREADY RUNNING (with the vulnerable config) when the agent
#     starts -- which is what makes "fixed the config but never restarted the
#     service" detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting the service cannot kill the
#     container / destroy the eval sample.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must RESTART the service, not merely start
# it if absent.
